  "rules": {
    "population": "Within each scene, contiguous disjoint PID ranges cover the scope from 1. The first group contains one tenth of the scene population and inherits the entire preceding scene (or D3's 100,000-process seed). Remaining groups split the remaining population in repeating weights 1,2,3,4,5; floor each share, then give the last group the remainder.",
    "summaries": "For zero-based group index i > 0: inbox = members * (i % 7); outbox = floor(members * (i % 5) / 3). If outbox > 0, oldestPendingSeconds = 60 + (i % 9) * 60 and oldestPendingPid = firstPid; otherwise both are null. Scene totals sum the groups and retain the maximum age with its source PID.",
    "coverage": "All values are synthetic assertions over unexpanded groups, not verified execution history. Null age here means no pending output in that synthetic group; unavailable age would require separate coverage metadata in a real contract.",
    "layout": "Group identities and ranges define membership only; the raster positions, cell counts, area and relief are illustrative, not a data-driven rendering."
